#heading(numbering: none)[Code and Data] <sec:code>

*Code.* #link("https://github.com/ShishirAravindan/cartel-succession")[github.com/ShishirAravindan/cartel-succession] (public). The pre-registrations are git tags (`prereg-p1`, `prereg-p1b`, `prereg-p1c`, `prereg-p23`, `prereg-p23b`), each committed before the runs it covers; the plan as registered is `docs/plan.md` at each tag.

*Data.* Every observation is generated by the simulation; we use no external dataset. The raw run logs (all 493 game runs, pilots and an excluded first attempt included; about 2.2 GB uncompressed) are a compressed archive attached to the repository's #link("https://github.com/ShishirAravindan/cartel-succession/releases/tag/v1.0")[v1.0 release]. Each game directory holds every model call (prompt, reasoning, notes and parsed price), the per-round prices, quantities and profits, its configuration and the git commit it ran on. The curated tables behind every number in the paper are in the repository (`seat_swap/results/`).

*What is ours and what is reused.* The repository is a fork of the sprint's starter repository. Reused without changes: `llm-cartel/`, the open implementation of #cite(<riemer2026>, form: "prose") (the logit Bertrand market and the pricing prompt of #cite(<fish2024>, form: "prose")); `util/`, the sprint's compute and inference routing; and `literature/`, the sprint's reading list. Ours: `seat_swap/` (succession code: branching a game from a snapshot, swapping a seat, choosing what the newcomer inherits, forcing prices; model serving on Modal with vLLM; metrics, tests, analysis scripts and figures), `seat_swap/results/` (curated tables) and `paper/` (this report's source).
